  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A typical summer time pattern will be in place\nthrough much the week with Bermuda High pressure centered off \nthe Southeast coast and a thermal trough across the piedmont. \nNear zonal flow aloft with a series of shortwave troughs \npushing across the area will result climo precip chances for \nthe next several days with best chances through peak heating and\nseabreeze related for the most part but will also depend on \ntiming and exact location of individual shortwave troughs. The \nsevere threat appears minimal for the next few days with \nlimited shear, though somewhat better shear develops toward the \nmiddle of the week. \n\nHot temperatures continue through the week as well with highs \nin the lower 90s inland into Monday, then warming in to the mid \n90s Tue/Wed and beyond. Temps generally in the mid to upper 80s \nalong the coast. The probabilities for Major Heat Risk increase \nto around 50-80% Monday through Thursday with highest probs on \nTuesday and Wednesday.",
